  "id": "tonic-immobility",
  "term": "tonic immobility",
  "definition": "Tonic immobility is an inborn, last-resort defensive response to a predator in which an animal becomes immobile. It is often linked with death-feigning but is described here as the final part of that broader set of behaviors rather than the whole pattern.",
